<p><strong>FINAL ELECTION RESULTS!</strong></p>
<p>On November 18, 2025, the City Council held a special session to certify the results of the November 4, 2025, General Election.<br />Those elected to office are:<br /><strong>Mayor </strong>&ndash; Zack Stratton<br /><strong>Councilmembers</strong> &ndash; David Lauret, Parker McCumber, and Jacob Wood.<br />In accordance with state code 10-3-201(2), they will take office on January 5, 2026, at 12 o&rsquo;clock noon.</p>
<p><strong>CASTING OF LOTS<br /></strong>On June 26, 2024, the Vineyard City Council voted to put a change in government to a vote of the people. At an election held on November 5, 2024, Vineyard Residents approved a change in government from a five-member council to a six-member council. As a result of the change in government and in accordance with Utah State Code 10-3b-606, those three (3) Council members were to be elected to office. Also, in accordance with Utah State Code 10-3b-6-606(4) of those three (3) Council members, one is to serve a two-year term, which is to be chosen by lot. This was done at the November 18, 2025, City Council Special Session. Parker McCumber drew the 2-year seat. David Lauret and Jacob Wood will retain the 4-year seat.</p>
<p><a href= "https://www.vineyardutah.gov/2025 General Election Certification.pdf?t=202511191345090"  target="_blank"  >Certification of the 2025 General Election</a></p>
<p>______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br />ELECTION RESULTS</p>
<p><a rel="noopener" href="https://electionresults.utah.gov/results/public/utah-county-ut/elections/general11042025" target="_blank">https://electionresults.utah.gov/results/public/utah-county-ut/elections/general11042025</a></p>
<p>______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br />We have two candidates who have withdrawn from the 2025 General Election, Hayden Morris (Council) and Hector Hernandez (Mayor). Their withdrawal forms can be found under their candidate information.&nbsp;<br />_______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br />General Election Results:<br />Utah County will be posting preliminary election results at 8:00pm and 10:00 PM on election day Tuesday, November 4, 2025.<br />Friday November 7, 2025 at 5:00 PM<br />Wednesday November 5, 2025 at 8:00 PM<br />Wednesday, November 12 at 5:00 PM<br />Friday November 14, 2025, at 5:00 PM<br />Tuesday November 18, 2025 at 12:00 PM<br />Official Canvass will be held on Tuesday November 18 at 6:00 PM<br />_______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br />With the official ballot drop box at City Hall (125 South Main Street, Vineyard, Utah) now open, we want to remind everyone that City Hall is now considered a voting location under Utah election law. As such, no electioneering is permitted within 150 feet of the drop box. This restriction helps ensure a neutral environment for voters and maintains the integrity of the election process.</p>
<p>For reference, <strong>Utah Code &sect;20A-3a-501(1)(a)</strong> defines <em>electioneering</em> as:</p>
<p><strong>&ldquo;Any oral, printed, or written attempt to persuade persons to refrain from voting or to vote for or vote against any candidate or issue.&rdquo;</strong></p>
<p>This includes, but is not limited to, displaying campaign signs (Including cars, bikes, etc.), distributing literature, wearing campaign apparel (Shirts, hats, buttons, etc.), or engaging in conversations intended to influence a voter&rsquo;s choice within the restricted area. We appreciate your cooperation in helping us maintain a fair and accessible voting environment for all residents. To help clarify where the restriction applies, below is a photo showing the approximate 150-foot boundary around City Hall. The marked area represents where <strong>no </strong>campaign activity or materials may be displayed while the ballot drop box is in operation.<br /><img /><img src="https://www.vineyardutah.gov/Recorder/150' Radius - Drop Box.png?t=202510281307340" alt="150' Radius - Drop Box" width="476" height="313" /></p>
<p>Additionally, on November 4, 2025, the City Hall building will be an active polling location, and the 150 feet restriction will apply to the City Hall building as well as the County drop box. Please see the map for the full restricted area.</p>
<p><strong><img src="https://www.vineyardutah.gov/Recorder/2025 Election/Electioneering 150 From Polling Location - Copy.jpg?t=202510281308560" alt="Electioneering 150 From Polling Location - Copy" width="463" height="451" /><br /><br /></strong></p>
<p>If you have any questions about the restricted area or how it is measured, please don&rsquo;t hesitate to contact the Recorder&rsquo;s Office at 385.338.5183.</p>
<p><strong>______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br /><a href= "../Notice_of_Drop_Boxes_d8ae6ba193.pdf?t=202510091124170"  target="_blank"  >Drop Box Locations</a><br />______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br /><a href= "../Notice_of_Early_Voting_88d98d58d5.pdf?t=202510091119420"  target="_blank"  >Early Voting Notice and Location</a><br />______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br /><a href= "../Notice_of_Logic_and_Accuracy_bd7c81b291.pdf?t=202510091123380"  target="_blank"  >Logic and Accuracy Testing</a><br />______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br /><a href= "https://www.vineyardutah.gov/Recorder/2025 Election/2025 NOTICE OF ELECTION 11.04.2025.pdf?t=202510061238360" rel="noopener"  target="_blank"  >General Election Notice</a><br /></strong></p>
<p>The Utah County Elections Division gives notice of the General Election that will be held on Tuesday, November 4, 2025.<br /><br />Voters must be citizens of the United States, residents of the voting precinct in which they are voting, and 18 years old or older by the date of the election to participate. All eligible voters will receive their ballot by mail approximately three weeks before Election Day.<br /><br />A sample ballot and other information relating to the election, including polling places, polling place hours, instructions regarding how an individual with a disability may obtain information on voting in an accessible manner, and qualifications of voters may be obtained from the following sources:<br />1. &nbsp; &nbsp;Visiting the Utah County Elections Division&rsquo;s website: https://vote.utahcounty.gov<br />2. &nbsp; &nbsp;Visiting the Statewide Electronic Voter Information Website: https://vote.utah.gov<br />3. &nbsp; &nbsp;Visiting the Utah County Elections Division Office<br />4. &nbsp; &nbsp;Calling the Utah County Elections Division: (801) 851-VOTE (8683)<br />5. &nbsp; &nbsp;Emailing the Utah County Elections Division: elections@utahcounty.gov<br />6. &nbsp; &nbsp;Contacting your City Recorder<br /><br />A public demonstration will be held to test the voting devices and tabulation equipment being used for the noticed election. Anyone who would like to witness the testing is invited to attend, beginning at 10:00 a.m. on October 9, 2025 at the Utah County Ballot Center - 100 E Center Street ROOM LL700 Provo Utah.<br /><br />All eligible voters will receive their ballot by mail approximately three weeks prior to Election Day.<br />We strongly encourage voters to return their ballots via the conveniently located drop boxes listed on our website at: vote.utahcounty.gov/voting-locations<br /><br />The Polling Locations (listed below) will be open from 7:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m. on Election Day for any voter in Utah County to return their ballot or vote in person. Accessible voting machines are available.</p>
