<p>DATE OF PUBLICATION: 9/30/2025<br />Posted on the following:<br />1. &nbsp; &nbsp;Utah Public Notice Website https://www.utah.gov/pmn<br />2. &nbsp; &nbsp;Utah County Website https://vote.utahcounty.gov/home<br />3. &nbsp; &nbsp;Utah County Admin Building bulletin board<br />&nbsp;<br /><strong>____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br /><a href= "https://www.vineyardutah.gov/Sample Ballot 2025 General Vineyard.pdf?t=202509081107420"  target="_blank"  >General Election - Sample Ballot</a><br />____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br /><a href="https://app.enhancedvoting.com/results/public/utah-county-ut/elections/primary08122025" target="_blank">Primary Election Results</a><br /></strong>Utah County will be posting preliminary election results at 8:00pm and 10:00 PM on election day Tuesday August 12, 2025.<br />Friday August 15, 2025 at 5:00 PM<br />Tuesday August 19, 2025 at 5:00 PM<br />and<br />Tuesday August 26, 2025 at 12:00 PM<br />Canvass will be done during a special session of the City Council on Tuesday August 26, 2025. The meeting will start at 6:00 PM.<strong><br /><br />________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br /><a href= "https://www.vineyardutah.gov/2025 Primary Election Notice.pdf?t=202507311334220"  target="_blank"  >Primary Election Notice</a><br />NOTICE OF VINEYARD 2025 MUNICIPAL PRIMARY ELECTION</strong><br />NOTICE OF ELECTION: A VINEYARD MUNICIPAL PRIMARY ELECTION WILL BE HELD IN UTAH<br />COUNTY ON AUGUST 12, 2025. INFORMATION RELATING TO THE ELECTION, INCLUDING<br />POLLING PLACES, POLLING PLACE HOURS, BALLOT DROP BOX LOCATIONS, AND<br />QUALIFICATIONS OF VOTERS MAY BE OBTAINED FROM THE FOLLOWING SOURCES:<br /><a href="https://vote.utahcounty.gov/home" target="_blank">WWW.UTAHCOUNTY.VOTE</a>; <a href="https://vote.utah.gov/" target="_blank">VOTE.UTAH.GOV</a>; UTAH COUNTY OFFICES AT 100 EAST CENTER<br />STREET, SUITE 3100, PROVO, UTAH 84606; OR BY CONTACTING THE ELECTIONS OFFICE AT<br />801-851-8128.THE ELECTION WILL BE PRIMARILY CONDUCTED BY MAIL; IN-PERSON<br />VOTING WILL BE AVAILABLE AND LOCATIONS CAN BE FOUND AT<br /><a href="https://vote.utahcounty.gov/home" target="_blank">WWW.UTAHCOUNTY.VOTE</a>; DROP BOXES WILL BE AVAILABLE FOR DEPOSITING MAIL-IN<br />BALLOTS UNTIL 8:00 P.M. ON ELECTION DAY; AND REGISTRATION BY PROVISIONAL BALLOT<br />WILL BE AVAILABLE AT ANY POLLING PLACE. AN INDIVIDUAL WITH A DISABILITY WHO IS<br />NOT ABLE TO VOTE A MANUAL BALLOT BY MAIL MAY OBTAIN INFORMATION ON VOTING<br />IN AN ACCESSIBLE MANNER FROM THE <a href="https://vote.utahcounty.gov/home" target="_blank">COUNTY'S WEBSITE</a>, BY CONTACTING THE COUNTY<br />CLERK, OR BY REVIEWING THE INFORMATION INCLUDED WITH A BALLOT MAILED TO THE<br />VOTER.<br />SAMPLE BALLOT: A SAMPLE BALLOT FOR UTAH COUNTY FOR THE UPCOMING MUNICIPAL<br />PRIMARY ELECTION TO BE HELD ON AUGUST 12, 2025, MAY BE OBTAINED FROM THE<br />FOLLOWING SOURCES: <a href="2025_election_information.php" target="_blank">WWW.VINEYARDUTAH.GOV</a>; <a href="https://vote.utahcounty.gov/home" target="_blank">WWW.UTAHCOUNTY.VOTE</a>; UTAH<br />COUNTY ELECTION OFFICE AT 100 EAST CENTER STREET, SUITE 3100, PROVO, UTAH 84606;<br />OR BY CONTACTING THE ELECTIONS OFFICE AT 801-851-8128.<br />EARLY VOTING: EARLY VOTING WILL BE CONDUCTED FOR THE UPCOMING MUNICIPAL<br />PRIMARY ELECTION. INFORMATION REGARDING THE DATES, TIMES, AND LOCATION OF<br />EARLY VOTING MAY BE OBTAINED FROM THE FOLLOWING SOURCES:<br /><a href="2025_election_information.php" target="_blank">WWW.VINEYARDUTAH.GOV</a>; <a href="https://vote.utahcounty.gov/home" target="_blank">WWW.UTAHCOUNTY.VOTE</a>; UTAH COUNTY ELECTIONS OFFICE<br />AT 100 EAST CENTER STREET, SUITE 3100, PROVO, UTAH 84606; VOTE.UTAH.GOV; OR BY<br />CONTACTING THE ELECTIONS OFFICE AT 801-851-8128.<br />FOR MORE ELECTION INFORMATION, INCLUDING CANDIDATE PROFILES, WHERE TO CHECK<br />YOUR VOTER INFORMATION, AND HOW TO VOTE, PLEASE VISIT<br /><a href="2025_election_information.php" target="_blank">https://www.vineyardutah.gov/government/2025_election_information.php.</a><br />Post: 7/31/2025 by: Pamela Spencer, City Recorder<strong><br />________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br />Ballots are in the mail!</strong> <br />If you don't receive yours by August 5 please contact Utah County Elections Office at 801.851.8128.<br /><strong><br />Track My Ballot<br /></strong>Track my ballot updates are based on certain process checkpoints. These checkpoints are when the ballot is mailed out by the county clerk, when the ballot is received back at the county office and when the ballot is accepted for tabulation.<strong><br /><br />Sign up for this free service by visiting: <a rel="noopener" href="https://trackmyballot.utah.gov/voter/" target="_blank">https://trackmyballot.utah.gov/voter/</a></strong><br />________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br /><a rel="noopener" href="https://www.utahcounty.gov/cms/uploads/Notice_of_Early_Voting_80df04783c.pdf" target="_blank">Utah County Early Voting Notice</a><br /><strong><br />Track My Ballot<br /></strong>Track my ballot updates are based on certain process checkpoints. These checkpoints are when the ballot is mailed out by the county clerk, when the ballot is received back at the county office and when the ballot is accepted for tabulation.<strong><br /><br />Sign up for this free service by visiting: <a href="https://trackmyballot.utah.gov/voter/" target="_blank">https://trackmyballot.utah.gov/voter/</a><br /></strong><br />________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br />Profiles submitted to the State website for those who are involved in the Primary Election are now live. Registered voters can go to <a href="https://votesearch.utah.gov/voter-search/search/search-by-address/candidates-and-issues or vote.utah.gov" target="_blank">https://votesearch.utah.gov/voter-search/search/search-by-address/candidates-and-issues</a> or <a href="https://vote.utah.gov/" target="_blank">vote.utah.gov</a> to search for candidates in their area.</p>
<p>Also the candidate profiles can be found here by clicking on the buttons above to find mayor and council candidates&rsquo; information.</p>
<p>________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br /><a href= "https://www.vineyardutah.gov/2025 Primary Vineyard Sample Ballot.pdf?t=202506261615500"  target="_blank"  >Vineyard 2025 Primary Election - Sample Ballot</a><br /><br /><br />Here are your candidates in ballot order:<br /><br /><strong>MAYOR (4-YEAR TERM)</strong><br />Zack Stratton<br />Mardi Sifuentes<br /><br /><strong>COUNCILMEMBER (4-YEAR TERM)</strong><br />Brett Clawson<br />Jacob Wood<br />Caden Rhoton<br />Terry Ewing<br />Ezra Nair<br />Parker McCumber<br />David Lauret<br />Steve Terry<br /><br />Vineyard will be holding a Primary Election on August 12, 2025, to nominate six (6) City Council candidates to move on to the General Election. You will be voting for up to three (3) people.&nbsp;<br /><br />________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br /><br /><strong><a href= "https://www.vineyardutah.gov/Important Dates to Remember.pdf?t=202506231532410"  target="_blank"  >Important Dates to Remember</a><br /><br />________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br />DECLARATION OF CANDIDACY<br /></strong><br />The Declaration of Candidacy Period begins Monday June 2 and runs through June 6, in the Vineyard Elections Office, 125 South Main Street. The hours will be Monday through Friday 8:00 am to 5:00 PM on a first-come, first-served basis (no appointment necessary). <em>See filing qualification below.</em><br /><br /><strong>ALL CANDIDATES MUST FILE IN PERSON!</strong><br />If you will out of the state for the entire week of the declaration period, please contact the City Recorder&rsquo;s office at 385.338.5183 or 385.432.7214 for further details. <br /><br />We ask that you bring the Conflict of Interest Form and if necessary, the Name Variation Form with you when you come in to&nbsp; file your declaration of candidacy.<br /><br /><a href= "https://www.vineyardutah.gov/Recorder/2025 Election/Sample Declaration Packet.pdf?t=202505291253100"  target="_blank"  >Sample Declaration Packet</a> - this a sample only. The Election's Office will provide you with the forms you will need to fill out.<br /><br /><a href= "https://www.vineyardutah.gov/Recorder/2025 Election/9 - Conflict of Interest Disclosure Statement - Vineyard updated 5.15.2025.pdf?t=202505151841160"  target="_blank"  >Conflict of Interest Disclosure Statement</a> - Please fill this form out and bring it with you when you come in to file your declaration of candidacy.<br /><br /><a href= "https://www.vineyardutah.gov/Recorder/2025 Election/4V - Candidate Name Variation Guide & Request.pdf?t=202505151842040"  target="_blank"  >Name Variation Guide and Form</a> - this form is only need if you wish to use a nick name or derivative of your legal first name. Please fill it out and bring it with you when you come in to file you declaration of candidacy.<br /><br /><a href= "https://www.vineyardutah.gov/Recorder/2025 Election/4N - Nomination Petition.pdf?t=202505291041410"  target="_blank"  >Nomination Petition Form</a>- this form is only needed if you are nominating someone to run for an elected office. This form must be turned in during the declaration period, June 2-6, 2025, 8 AM to 5 PM.<br /><strong>_____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br /><br />2025 VINEYARD CITY MUNICIPAL ELECTION NOTICE</strong></p>
<p>Pursuant to Section 10-3-301(2)(a) of the <u>Utah Code</u>, notice is hereby given that the Municipal Offices in Vineyard, Utah to be voted on in the 2025 Municipal General Election are:</p>
<ul>
<li>Mayor &ndash; to be elected at-large to serve a four-year term.</li>
<li>City Council Members &ndash; three (3) council members will be elected at-large to serve a four-year term with the exception that one member will serve a two-year term. The two-year term will be determined by lots immediately following the election canvass. (UCA 10-3b-606(4))</li>
</ul>
<p>A Primary Election will be held, if necessary, on Tuesday, August 12, 2025. The General Election will be held on November 4, 2025.</p>
<p>A Vineyard City resident who is interested in becoming a candidate must file a Declaration of Candidacy between <u>June 2 and June 6, 2025</u>. Declarations of Candidacy must be filed,<strong><em> in person</em></strong>, with the Vineyard City Recorder's Office at Vineyard City Hall, 125 South Main Street, Vineyard, Utah, Monday through Friday, 8 am to 5 pm. A $50.00 filing fee is due at the time of filing.</p>
<p><em>Election information may be obtained at:</em></p>
<ul>
<li>Vineyard City Recorder&rsquo;s Office: Pamela Spencer 338.5183, <a rel="noopener" href="mailto:pams@vineyardutah.gov" target="_blank">pams@vineyardutah.gov</a> or Tony Lara 385.432.7214, <a rel="noopener" href="mailto:tonyl@vineyardutah.gov" target="_blank">tonyl@vineyardutah.gov</a></li>
<li>Utah County website: <a rel="noopener" href="https://vote.utahcounty.gov/home" target="_blank">https://vote.utahcounty.gov/home</a></li>
<li>Utah State website: <a rel="noopener" href="https://vote.utah.gov/" target="_blank">https://vote.utah.gov</a></li>
</ul>
<h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2"><strong><span style="font-size: 16px;">________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________<br />Filing Qualifications</span></strong></h3>
<p>A person filing a declaration of candidacy for a city office must be (per&nbsp;<a onclick="return showExternalSiteDialog(this);" onkeypress="this.onclick();" rel="noopener" href="https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title20A/Chapter9/20A-9-S201.html" target="_blank" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message" aria-label="Utah Code Section 20A-9-201 Opens in new window">Utah Code Section 20A-9-201</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a onclick="return showExternalSiteDialog(this);" onkeypress="this.onclick();" rel="noopener" href="https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title20A/Chapter9/20A-9-S203.html" target="_blank" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message" aria-label="203 Opens in new window">203</a>):</p>
<ul>
<li>A United States citizen at the time of filing;</li>
<li>A resident of Vineyard City for the 12 consecutive months immediately preceding the date of the election (or a resident of an area recently annexed into Vineyard City);</li>
<li>A registered voter.</li>
</ul>
<p>In accordance with&nbsp;<a onclick="return showExternalSiteDialog(this);" onkeypress="this.onclick();" rel="noopener" href="https://le.utah.gov/xcode/ArticleIV/Article_IV,_Section_6.html?v=UC_AIV_S6_1800010118000101" target="_blank" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message" aria-label="Utah Constitution Article IV, Section 6 Opens in new window">Utah Constitution Article IV, Section 6</a>, any mentally incompetent person, any person convicted of a felony, or any person convicted of treason or a crime against the elective franchise may not hold office in this state until the right to hold elective office is restored under&nbsp;<a onclick="return showExternalSiteDialog(this);" onkeypress="this.onclick();" rel="noopener" href="https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title20A/Chapter2/20A-2-S101.3.html#:~:text=Convicted%20misdemeanants%20%2D%2D%20Restoration%20of%20right%20to%20vote%20or%20hold%20office.,-(1)&amp;text=As%20used%20in%20this%20section,an%20offense%20under%20this%20title.&amp;text=has%20successfully%20completed%20the%20term,which%20the%20misdemeanant%20was%20sentenced." target="_blank" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message" aria-label="Utah Code Section 20A-2-101.3 Opens in new window">Utah Code Section 20A-2-101.3</a>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<a onclick="return showExternalSiteDialog(this);" onkeypress="this.onclick();" rel="noopener" href="https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title20A/Chapter2/20A-2-S101.5.html#:~:text=%2D2%2D101.5.-,Convicted%20felons%20%2D%2D%20Restoration%20of%20right,and%20right%20to%20hold%20office.&amp;text=As%20used%20in%20this%20section,court%20of%20the%20United%20States.&amp;text=the%20felon%20has%20successfully%20completed,which%20the%20felon%20was%20sentenced." target="_blank" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message" aria-label="Section 20A-2-101.5 Opens in new window">Section 20A-2-101.5</a>.</p>


